n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn. \n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"] [:db/cas 17592186420352 :question/problem "Find $7det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -0.5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find $7det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -0.5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186420352 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1\\cdot 2=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7det(A)-2det(B)=7\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-6)=12.$" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1\\cdot 2=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7det(A)-2det(B)=7\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-6)=12.$"] [:db/cas 17592186420353 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **II.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **II.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186420353 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186420414 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 